From: =?UTF-8?q?Bj=C3=B6rn=20Stierand?= <bjoern-github@innovention.de>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:50:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(keygen): read rbw history result with sh 2.x

sh 2.0 returns a plain str unless _return_cmd is set, so accessing
exit_code and stderr raised AttributeError and bw-keygen could not
detect an existing vault entry.
---
 bw-askpass | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bw-askpass b/bw-askpass
index 13cb8db..f469ccd 100755
--- a/bw-askpass
+++ b/bw-askpass
@@ -19,7 +19,11 @@ def bw_get(key: Path):
 
 
 def bw_exists(key: Path):
-    history_cmd = rbw("history", *RBW_ARGS, key.name, _ok_code=[0, 1])
+    # sh >= 2.0 returns a plain str instead of a RunningCommand unless
+    # _return_cmd is set, so exit_code/stderr are only available this way.
+    history_cmd = rbw(
+        "history", *RBW_ARGS, key.name, _ok_code=[0, 1], _return_cmd=True
+    )
     return history_cmd.exit_code == 0 or b"no entry found" not in history_cmd.stderr
 
 
